{
  "about": [
    "Signature shots (V4, 2026-11-26): every unit fires its faction's look (src/fx-kinds/signature.js).",
    "palettes: each faction's energy colours (RGB 0..1, additive glows; `deep` is the dark underlay that keeps a glow readable on snow, sand and lava).",
    "families: the slot a unit type falls back to when its faction has no entry for the type itself (a Rider lent to Ashfall fires Ashfall's ranger look).",
    "factions: unit type or family -> look id. A type with no entry and no family keeps its own look (creatures, bosses, Iron units, bombers, flamers, medics).",
    "looks: kind (signature-kinds.js), palette keys, impact (signature-impacts.js) and sizes as [metres, CSS-pixel floor] pairs: a size never draws smaller than its floor at any zoom.",
    "sheets: the Codex flipbooks (codex-vfx3/, packed by tools/pack-fx-atlas.py: flight loop `<name>` at 64 px frames, impact `<name>Hit` at 128 px), all normal alpha, fps from codex-vfx3/README.md; `head` is where the ball sits in a flight frame (put on the round), `cell` the flight quad as [metres, desktop px floor, phone px floor] (square), `hard` steps frames without cross-fading (spinners), `fade`/`grow` shape the impact, `upright` keeps the hoop within that many degrees of screen-vertical (mirrored rather than turned past it); a look without its sheet in the atlas (or before the sheets load) draws the procedural cells."
  ],
